o><mjx-msub space=\"4\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D707 TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi><mjx-script style=\"vertical-align: -0.15em;\"><mjx-mi class=\"mjx-i\" size=\"s\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c1D45B TEX-I\"></mjx-c></mjx-mi></mjx-script></mjx-msub></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mo>⋯</mo><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></span>.</li>\n<li>Explain in one or two sentences why <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"thm-loewner-basic\">@thm-loewner-basic</span> (b) could not\nbe extended to intermediate eigenvalues by the argument Chapter 13 used,\nand what <span class=\"citation\" data-cites=\"thm-courant-fischer\">@thm-courant-fischer</span> supplies\ninstead.</li>\n</ol>\n</div>","file":"ch17-variational/02-courant-fischer.html"}